.nh
.TH "TAKO" "1" "Jun 2026" "Tako CLI" "Tako CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
tako-heal-pause - Pause self-healing for the environment or one service


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtako heal pause [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Pause self-healing on every server of the environment (or --server). The
pause defaults to 1h; --for sets another duration (at most 7 days) and
--until-resume pauses until tako heal resume. A pause waits for an action
already running and is in effect when the command returns.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--for\fP=1h0m0s
	Pause duration (at most 168h)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for pause

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	One server only

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--service\fP=""
	One service only

.PP
\fB--until-resume\fP[=false]
	Pause until tako heal resume


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default is ./tako.yaml or ./tako.json)

.PP
\fB-e\fP, \fB--env\fP=""
	environment to use (default: the only environment, else production, else the first alphabetically)

.PP
\fB--events\fP=""
	stream progress events to stdout: ndjson (human output moves to stderr)

.PP
\fB--host-key-mode\fP=""
	SSH host key verification mode: tofu, strict, ask (default: tofu)

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	output format: text or json (json reserves stdout for the final result document)

.PP
\fB--preview\fP=""
	preview environment to use (deploy, ps, logs, exec, history, rollback, config explain); -e then names its base

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtako-heal(1)\fP
